    "result_text": "All changes are complete and the test suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the string `membershipTier` with a numeric `membershipLevel` (1\u20133), computed at creation as `1 + (email present) + (namesakeCount == 0)`, capped at 3.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Replaced the `membershipTier` (string) schema property with `membershipLevel` (integer, `int32`, min 1, max 3, read-only). Since DTOs are generated from this spec at build time, `OwnerDto` now exposes `membershipLevel` and no longer has `membershipTier`.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a derived `getMembershipLevel()` that starts at 1, adds 1 for a present email, adds 1 when `namesakeCount` is 0, and caps at 3. Because it reads the email and namesakeCount fixed at creation, it always returns the creation-time level. Also updated the stale \"GOLD tier\" comment.\n\n3. **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Removed the old `membershipTier` MapStruct expression (the GOLD/SILVER/BRONZE logic). MapStruct now auto-maps `membershipLevel` from the new getter.\n\n4. **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 Updated the create audit line to record `membershipLevel={}` (using `owner.getMembershipLevel()`, evaluated after email and namesakeCount are set), and refreshed the now-stale tier doc comment.\n\n5. **`rest/controller/v2/OwnerRestControllerV2.java`** \u2014 Updated a doc comment that referenced the removed GOLD tier behaviour.\n\nThe new test `coreNumericLevel` (email + unique name \u2192 level 3) passes, and no `membershipTier`/BRONZE/SILVER/GOLD references remain.",
